 "reading": {
  "headline": "At the measured commit every speculative arm is slower than its matched AR arm on this workload: -20.3% decode rate at c=1 natural lengths, -18.7% at c=4, -13.3% at c=2 long prompts, and -11.3% at c=1 with the 128-token override. Inter-token latency degrades in the same direction (84 ms -> 119 ms at c=1).",
  "superseded_by_control": "The slowdown is a regression in the speculative path, not a property of speculative decoding on this workload. On the control tree (f607e3184, 085bdd86b~1) the same six requests with the same flags decode at 23.60 tok/s against 11.79 tok/s for true AR (2.00x), where this tree's automatic arm decodes at 9.37 tok/s. AR is unchanged between the trees (11.79 vs 11.75), so the whole difference is on the MTP side. The control tree is not exact in general: on seven natural prompts, sequential and without prefix reuse, its two arms agree byte-for-byte on five and diverge at tokens 47 and 155 on the other two, so its speed is real but its output identity is not universal. See 2026-09-18-gfx1151-qwen38-mtp-exactness-regression.json.",
  "acceptance": "Accepted drafts per cycle are 0.10-0.24 on this content at this commit, against 0.44-0.89 recorded for the mtp-bench prompt classes, so a cycle that spends four verifier rows to commit ~1.1-1.25 tokens cannot pay for itself. The exact tree's 2.00x at the same acceptance-free conditions shows the acceptance collapse and the slowdown share the regression's cause.",
  "concurrency": "At c=4 only 2 of 8 requests ran MTP and 26.3% of tokens were speculative; the provider refuses under contention. The mixed-route coupling run measures the same effect with a true-AR control inside one load.",
  "identity": "Greedy output is not stable between the arms at this commit: AR and MTP diverge after 5-7 tokens on every prompt tested, including a trivial one. Two AR runs and two MTP runs are each bit-identical, so this is a path difference, not nondeterminism.",
  "status": "Diagnostic. Not a retained performance claim: it measures a broken speculative route on a superseded commit."
 },
